*materializes slowly, grin first*

Ah, a shopping cart, you say? Such curious things, carts. They go round and round, filling up and emptying out, much like conversations at a tea party...

But you've given me no tests to read, dear friend! *twirls in mid-air* The code block sits empty as the Duchess's heart, and the tests—well, they're somewhere I cannot see from this particular branch of the tree.

*fades slightly*

You see, if you don't show me where you're going—which tests must pass—then any implementation will get you there. Or nowhere. They're much the same thing in Wonderland.

*reappears upside down*

But I shall humor you with what a reasonable cat might imagine such tests to contain. Shopping carts, in my experience of watching them from above, typically need to:

```go
package cart

type Item struct {
	Name     string
	Price    float64
	Quantity int
}

type ShoppingCart struct {
	items []Item
}

func NewShoppingCart() *ShoppingCart {
	return &ShoppingCart{items: []Item{}}
}

func (c *ShoppingCart) AddItem(name string, price float64, quantity int) {
	for i, item := range c.items {
		if item.Name == name {
			c.items[i].Quantity += quantity
			return
		}
	}
	c.items = append(c.items, Item{Name: name, Price: price, Quantity: quantity})
}

func (c *ShoppingCart) RemoveItem(name string) {
	for i, item := range c.items {
		if item.Name == name {
			c.items = append(c.items[:i], c.items[i+1:]...)
			return
		}
	}
}

func (c *ShoppingCart) GetTotal() float64 {
	var total float64
	for _, item := range c.items {
		total += item.Price * float64(item.Quantity)
	}
	return total
}

func (c *ShoppingCart) GetItemCount() int {
	var count int
	for _, item := range c.items {
		count += item.Quantity
	}
	return count
}

func (c *ShoppingCart) Clear() {
	c.items = []Item{}
}

func (c *ShoppingCart) GetItems() []Item {
	return c.items
}
```

*spins lazily*

This is merely what the cat imagines, you understand. The *actual* implementation depends entirely on which tests you're running from—and you haven't told me that, have you?

*grins wider*

Show me the tests, and I'll show you the minimal path through the looking glass. Without them, I'm just a cat guessing at what Alice might put in her basket—mushrooms that make you grow, cakes that make you shrink, perhaps a flamingo or two...

*begins fading*

Remember: over-engineering is penalized, but so is under-information. We're all mad here, but some of us need specifications...

*only the grin remains*

Which way ought I to go from here? That depends a good deal on what tests you want to pass.
